Prefix: : <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/temporal-qualification#>
Prefix: xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

Ontology: <https://finsight-tech.com/ontology/examples/temporal-qualification>


# ************************************************************************
# Temporal Qualification of Financial Meaning
# ************************************************************************
#
# Distinguishes occurrence time, effective time, validity intervals and
# system-recorded time. The examples show that temporal context belongs to
# the financial meaning whose truth changes, not automatically to the thing.
#

Datatype: xsd:dateTime

### Core financial concepts

Class: BusinessEvent

Class: AmendmentEvent
    SubClassOf: BusinessEvent

Class: Contract

Class: ContractTerms

Class: Settlement

Class: SettlementCondition

Class: OutstandingSettlementCondition
    SubClassOf: SettlementCondition

Class: Portfolio

Class: LegalEntity

Class: Security

Class: RatingAssessment

Class: TimeInstant

Class: TimePeriod

Class: SystemRecord

Class: ContractTermsRecord
    SubClassOf: SystemRecord


### Occurrence time

ObjectProperty: occurredAt
    Domain: BusinessEvent
    Range: TimeInstant


### Effective time

# The amendment event occurs at one time, while the resulting terms may
# become effective at another time.

ObjectProperty: establishesTerms
    Domain: AmendmentEvent
    Range: ContractTerms

ObjectProperty: termsOf
    Domain: ContractTerms
    Range: Contract

ObjectProperty: effectiveFrom
    Domain: ContractTerms
    Range: TimeInstant


### Settlement condition episode

Class: SettlementConditionEpisode
    SubClassOf:
        conditionOf exactly 1 Settlement,
        hasCondition exactly 1 SettlementCondition

ObjectProperty: conditionOf
    Domain: SettlementConditionEpisode
    Range: Settlement

ObjectProperty: hasCondition
    Domain: SettlementConditionEpisode
    Range: SettlementCondition


### Time-bounded management participation

Class: ManagementParticipation
    SubClassOf:
        manager exactly 1 LegalEntity,
        subject exactly 1 Portfolio

ObjectProperty: manager
    Domain: ManagementParticipation
    Range: LegalEntity

ObjectProperty: subject
    Domain: ManagementParticipation
    Range: Portfolio


### Rating assessment

ObjectProperty: assesses
    Domain: RatingAssessment
    Range: Security


### Validity interval

# validDuring intentionally has no global Domain here. It can qualify
# different contextual concepts such as a condition episode, participation
# or rating assessment without implying that those concepts are the same kind.

ObjectProperty: validDuring
    Range: TimePeriod


### System-recorded time

# recordedAt describes when a system representation was recorded. It is
# not automatically the time at which the underlying financial fact became true.

DataProperty: recordedAt
    Domain: SystemRecord
    Range: xsd:dateTime


### Recorded representation

ObjectProperty: recordsTerms
    Domain: ContractTermsRecord
    Range: ContractTerms


### Focused temporal semantics

Class: OutstandingSettlementEpisode
    SubClassOf:
        SettlementConditionEpisode,
        hasCondition exactly 1 OutstandingSettlementCondition,
        validDuring exactly 1 TimePeriod

Class: TemporallyQualifiedManagementParticipation
    SubClassOf:
        ManagementParticipation,
        validDuring exactly 1 TimePeriod

Class: TemporallyQualifiedRatingAssessment
    SubClassOf:
        RatingAssessment,
        validDuring exactly 1 TimePeriod


### Modelling boundaries

# AmendmentEvent
#     occurredAt -> TimeInstant
#
# ContractTerms
#     effectiveFrom -> TimeInstant
#
# SettlementConditionEpisode
#     validDuring -> TimePeriod
#
# ContractTermsRecord
#     recordedAt -> xsd:dateTime
#
# These temporal relationships answer different questions:
#
# occurredAt    - when did the occurrence happen?
# effectiveFrom - when did the resulting financial meaning begin to apply?
# validDuring   - during what interval did a fact or relationship hold?
# recordedAt    - when did a system record the representation?
#
# A financial date such as maturityDate or paymentDate is a different kind
# of meaning again. Such dates are not modelled here as temporal validity.